{ "cls": "culture", "html": `<div class="culture">
    <span class="c-label">🎤 K-POP TIP</span>
    <h3>No Matter What — Idols Travel for Their Fans</h3>
    <p>K-pop idols don't only appear on big city stages. Many make time to visit <b>지역 팬들</b> (regional fans) in small towns — even when it means a <b>밤새</b> (all-night) drive. That devotion lives in Korean grammar: "<b>밤새도 갈 거예요</b>" (I'll go even if it takes all night), "<b>아무리 힘들더라도 노래할게요</b>" (no matter how hard it is, I'll sing), and "<b>팬분들을 만나야만 행복해요</b>" (only by meeting fans am I happy). Concession shows they won't quit, and restriction shows what they live for.</p>
    <div class="c-tip">✍️ Next time you promise something big, sound like a determined idol: "<b>늦더라도, 힘들더라도 꼭 갈게요!</b>" (Even if it's late, even if it's hard, I'll definitely go!) And when only one thing makes a dream real, say "<b>노력해야만 꿈을 이룰 수 있어요!</b>" (Only by working hard can you reach your dream!)</div>
  </div>` }
